        <body>
            <div xml:id="d579">

                <pb facs="0627" n="577" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg577"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr. Taylor.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-12-02"><hi rendition="#italic">December 2,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Our consul-general at Havana has telegraphed that the custom-house has embargoed
                    $3,000 worth of sugar belonging to Hidalgo &amp; Co., to pay fines. The fines
                    imposed upon the Ward Line of steamers are for mere clerical errors in manifests
                    from which Spanish vessels in our ports are exempt. Ask that intendente be
                    requested by telegraph to report facts to Madrid for decision. Inform Department
                    by cable of action taken.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
